Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: the emergency dialer follows dark mode, in two inks

The emergency dialer took its colours from the lock screen wallpaper: the
background from the wallpaper's main colour and the text from whether that
colour is light or dark. A dark wallpaper in light mode gave a black
dialer, a light one in dark mode a white dialer, while the emergency
information screen it opens follows dark mode, so the two did not match.
It is now white with black text in light mode and black with white text in
dark mode, and the wallpaper is not read. The background is opaque; at
90 percent over the wallpaper it showed as a dither on e-ink. The green
dial button is an outlined circle in the two inks, with no shadow.

The emergency information box took 155dp of a 576dp screen: an 80dp box
with 35dp above and 40dp below (values-h535dp, the bucket this phone
uses). The dialpad under it then lost the space kept for the dial button,
and the button sat on the 0. The margins are now 12dp above and below in
every height bucket. Its outline was white at 25 percent in light mode,
invisible on white, and grey at 52 percent in dark mode over a #202124
fill: it is now a 2dp border in the ink on the paper. The tap-again state
was a solid red box with white text; it is the same box with a 4dp
border, and the text is in the ink.
